      "text": "No, the higher specific activity of **T212S** does not mean it has a higher product titer. \n\nAccording to the data in **P152**, while **T212S** exhibits a higher specific activity (2.40 U/mg) compared to **A163V** (1.50 U/mg), it actually results in a lower product titer (3.90 g/L) than **A163V** (4.60 g/L) [Synthetic BioDesign eval: EctD primary + CelluWeave novel domain / literature / P152.pdf](biodesign-citation:citation-1). This demonstrates that enzyme activity and fermentation titer are separate outcomes and do not necessarily correlate linearly in this system.",
